\f1\fs22 He was extremely good at this. Whatever else may be said about Jamison Hardy, and there is a great deal, he could cost a thing. He worked in cubic metres. Ultra-high-performance concrete at ten metres over the whole footprint, plus the shafts, plus the cap on the lift head, plus the standing charge on the plant, plus the premium for continuous pour, because a cold joint is a seam and a seam is a thing that can be opened. He did the sums twice, once at the contract rate and once at the rate he intended to pay, and the difference between them was, by itself, more money than everyone downstairs would earn between them in their entire lives.\
Outside and four levels below him, the contractors had been on site since the previous afternoon. They had been engaged eleven days earlier. Hardy had signed the engagement himself, on the same day the labs had first flagged, in a routine progress note buried in a monthly, that they were seeing something interesting on the platform.
